    "reading": "With 85 holdout draws the lab3 tests have ~5% power at sigma=0.05, ~22% at 0.10, ~60% at 0.15, ~90% at 0.20 (log-propensity sd). The observed holdout gain makes sigma>=0.20 unlikely (P=0.02) and sigma=0.15 marginal (P=0.12). So a ball bias of sigma<=0.1 (best ball ~20% more likely than average) could have been missed. Its value if real: estimated top-6 picks give ~1.39 vs 1.33 hits/draw (+4%) and ~1.6x jackpot probability for the chosen set (vs 2.3x for an oracle); with sigma=0 (equally consistent with data) the gain is exactly zero, while hot numbers are the popular ones (prize-share loss is validated). Undetectable single-number biases up to +37% (pre-specified) or +56% (any of 27) are possible in principle with 169 draws."
